Description: Fix protoc-gen-js libc++ runtime linking
 protoc-gen-js links with -nostdlib++ but doesn't explicitly depend on libc++,
 causing undefined symbol errors for std::__Cr:: symbols at task 1635/76523.
 .
 This patch adds an explicit GN dependency on //buildtools/third_party/libc++
 to link against the bundled libc++ library (which has __Cr namespace matching
 the perfetto __config_site used during compilation).
 .
 Build 130 used deps (failed - stub BUILD.gn has sources=[]).
 Build 131 used libs=["c++"] (progress +31 tasks, but namespace mismatch).
 Build 132 uses deps with real bundled libc++ BUILD.gn.
 .
 Error: ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: std::__Cr::__libcpp_verbose_abort
        ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: std::__Cr::basic_string...
        ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: std::__Cr::ios_base::init
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-11

--- a/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
@@ -16,6 +16,9 @@ if (current_toolchain == host_toolchain) {
     deps = [
       "//third_party/protobuf:protoc_lib",

+      # Debian: Explicitly link bundled libc++ when using -nostdlib++
+      "//buildtools/third_party/libc++",
+
       # Default manifest on Windows (a no-op elsewhere).
       "//build/win:default_exe_manifest",
     ]
